   141	    - **Practical lead:** a − b ≥ max(3, 15% of N) and a ≥ 2b. Every guardrail subgroup must meet its frozen minimum and pass under both
   142	      countings.
   143	    - **Practical loss:** the mirror of the lead, or a guardrail breach confirmed under both countings.
   144	    - **No practical winner:** everything else, including a verdict a split could change, or a guardrail that was not exercised.
   145	    - **Too small:** fewer than 20 distinct matters, or fewer than 30 distinct questions per system per draw.
   146	    - **Invalid:** a planted wrong answer accepted, fewer than 3 of 4 supported controls accepted, or fewer than 2 of 3 repeats marked the same.
   147	- **The guardrails:** the unsupported share for figures, the unsupported share for yes/no questions, and the not-worth-tracking share, none
   148	  more than 10 points above the old system's. D428's original limits are printed beside them.
   149	- **Printed beside the verdict, not deciding:** a sign test and an interval (illustrative unless the frozen grouping supports them); the
   150	  frozen-reference reading of 07-01 to 07-14 (D431, superseded on this point only); and the proposed absolute floors.
   151	- **Kept from the earlier gates:**
   152	  - **The six lines of D400** are measured and reported on every ladder run. They no longer block release.
   153	  - **The parts code decides stay hard checks:** figure ranges meet end to end; the favourable end is the same across sends; the due day is
   154	    consistent in at least nine of ten.
   155	  - **Step 2's three checks stay,** as D427 and D431 set them.
   156	  - **Stage B's control line waits** with D658.
   157	- **Back to Alex,** before any release engineering resumes:
   158	  - a practical lead, with the split cards for his spot check;
   159	  - a practical loss, at once (D544);
   160	  - no practical winner, too small, or invalid, with the counts;
   161	  - no verdict by 2026-12-01.
   162	
   163	| Earlier gate | Now |
   164	|---|---|
   165	| 1. The ladder step (Stage A), Alex's six lines (D400) | Reported on every run. Its code-decidable parts are hard checks. Not passed in nine readings |
   166	| 2. The judge on the system's own questions (Stage B, D428) | Its unsupported shares become the comparison's guardrails. Its control line waits (D658). Not passed: 4 of 8 controls |
   167	| 3. End to end against the running pipeline (D427, D431) | **The comparison above.** The frozen-reference reading is printed beside it |
   168	| 4. Use on unseen news (D484) | Folded into the comparison, which runs on unseen weeks. Its proposed lines are printed beside it |
   261	                raise Leak(f'a request on {day} judges {view_id}, not a view this replay built a prompt for')
   262	            if shown != selected_by_view[view_id]:
   263	                raise Leak(f'{view_id} on {day}: the request shows {shown}, the selection was {selected_by_view[view_id]}')
   264	            response = self.budget.send(provider, request)
   265	            with self.budget.lock:
   266	                self.sent.append({'day': day, 'seq': seq, 'view': view_id, 'shown': shown})
   267	            return response
   268	        item = {'input_id': f'day:{day}', 'publication_day': day}
   269	        judging.evidence_in_view = recording_selection
   270	        try:
   271	            judged = judging.round_of_judgements(self.archive, self.cfg, self.conn, sorted(changed), seq, item, transport=watching)
   272	        finally:
   273	            judging.evidence_in_view = production_selection
   274	        self.conn.commit()
   275	        self.counts['judgements'] += len(judged)
   276	        return judged
