## Part A — Reading tools

All six permitted `run.json` identities match. The native-ID sample, redo selection, prior-round debate, confirmed plants, split tally and the card’s own position in the opening order are fixed. I accept D675’s readings of the frozen rule. [Eligibility](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/eligibility.py:60) · [D675](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:9729)

- **The scorer still trusts the flags that decide which cards count.** It re-reads the key but compares only question IDs. In memory, changing six `guardrail` flags flipped a practical loss to a lead with every input file unchanged. Take `guardrail`, `covering` and answer type from the verified key. [Scorer](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/score_comparison.py:158)
- **Timing can pass with incomplete evidence.** A missing attempt log counts as zero attempts, and the writer can lose a log line after recording the charge. Reconcile settled attempts with ledger totals. Where timing cannot be established, report a diagnostic. [Eligibility](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/eligibility.py:70) · [Ledger](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py:101)
- **Theme context still loses meaning.** The card drops the update marker and shows only the chosen condition. In two historical stores, 29 of 52 theme reasons cited another rung. Preserve the marker and show the numbered conditions those reasons refer to, without raw IDs. [Judge request](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:149) · [Card builder](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/build_cards.py:89)

NOT READY: verify scoring flags and attempt-log completeness, and render the theme references.

## Part B — §1.6 design

- **D400 and Step 2 line 2 have usable inputs.** Run the D400 collector per draw because it reads one ladder folder and its packet files. Treat a skipped ladder as unmeasured. For line 2, join each accepted repeat to its recorded `repeat_of` and retain the frozen third-reader rule. [D400 check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/d400_code_check.py:19) · [Collector](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/stage_a/collect_readings.py:38) · [Repeat record](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step2/compare.py:109)
- **Line 1 needs independent labels.** Lexical and party searches provide independent candidates but can miss the same pairs the product misses. Restore the earlier generator-miss audit. Remove the merge prompt’s claim that each candidate was already filed as a repeat. Freeze the labels before checking product retrieval. [Design](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/DESIGN-1.6.md:27) · [Audit](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step2-validation-2026-11-07/LOG.md:39) · [Prompt](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/clean-step2-forward-2026-11-08/merge-prompt-1.md:3)
- **Line 3 needs the paired dossier test.** Both renderers exist. Hold the surrounding dossier and independent detail key fixed, vary grouping alone, and compare paired detail totals. The proposed zero-loss rule is stricter than the recorded “no fewer” test. [Renderers](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step3/library.py:135) · [Recorded test](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step2-validation-2026-11-07/LOG.md:305)
- **D431 needs a recorded method decision.** Use the stores’ existing as-of readers for July 14. The no-adapter comparison can report agreement on the answers actually given, but D395’s seven-question score used ruler wording and ladders. Record the substitution and freeze comparability rules before reading. [As-of readers](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:118) · [D395](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4303)
- **Keep the verdict and release status separate.** “Practical lead” can coexist with “no release: hard check.” The floors can be computed from the cards. Assign the remaining report items, including D428 limits, illustrative statistics and time to opening. [Plan](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v12.md:219) · [Frozen report](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/verdict-rule.json:77)

CHANGE: fix Step 2’s labels and paired test, record the D431 substitution, and complete the report wiring.
